## It's More than Maintenance, It's Mission Assurance!

Are you a recent graduate who is passionate about aviation and eager to join the fast-paced world of Aircraft Maintenance? The sky is the limit with PAL Technical Services, a division of PAL Aerospace, and we are here to help kick-start your career!

At PAL, we believe in the future of our employees. Offering both dynamic and diverse career opportunities at our Canadian and international bases, PAL Technical Services is the perfect place to hone your skills, develop meaningful connections, and grow your career to new heights!

With safety at the forefront of our company culture, and honouring our core values of integrity and excellence, there has never been a better time to join our elite team of aviation professionals across our locations as a Non-certifying Aircraft Maintenance Engineer (Apprentice)!

## What to Expect:

• PAL Airlines Flight Line: Daily line maintenance support for Eastern Canada's largest regional carrier, includes layover checks up to A-checks, expert troubleshooting, engine changes, and propeller replacements
• St. John's, NL

• PAL Aerospace Flight Line: Serving our special mission aircrafts, our teams assist in the success of our airborne ISR services in Canada and abroad.
• Halifax, NS

• PAL Aerospace Modifications: Full aircraft design, customization and installation services to missionizing aircraft for search and rescue and surveillance operations, to aircraft conversions.
• St. John's, NL

## What We're Looking For:

• Transport Canada approved Aircraft Maintenance Course completed or have equivalent experience through a program such as ICS;
• Transport Canada Accrediation is preferred.

• Previous experience in an aviation role is considered an asset;

• The ability to work both independently and in a team environment;

• Strong communication, decision-making, troubleshooting, and organization skills.

PAL Group of Companies values its employees and offers a competitive benefits package.

## The Perks of being one of our PALs:

• Personal travel privileges with PAL and interline agreements with multiple airlines;

• Industry discounts;

• Comprehensive health benefits including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance;

• Pension Plan with Employer Matching;

• Employee Stock Purchase Plan;

• Employee Tuition Assistance Program;

• Employee and Family Assistance Programs.

## PAL Perks for AMEs:

• AME License Reimbursement Program;

• Type Course/Endorsement Training Opportunities;

• Personal travel privileges on most major airlines;

• Opportunities for internal growth.

Looking to see PAL employees in action? Click HERE to see what our team is capable of.

Applications for Non-certifying Aircraft Maintenance Engineers (Apprentices) with our Maintenance, Structures and Avionics teams will be accepted on an ongoing basis.

PAL Technical Services is committed to fostering an inclusive work environment that celebrates and encourages diversity, equity, and inclusion whereby individuals are recognized, supported, and respected. Candidates of all backgrounds are encouraged to apply.

Only those candidates selected for an interview will be contacted. Thank you.

