## Electrical Project Manager
Dartmouth, NS
AM - BKM - 9789

Meridia Recruitment Solutions has partnered with Black & McDonald, to find their next Electrical Project Manager to join their team in Dartmouth, Nova Scotia.

Black & McDonald is a leading integrated, multi-trade service provider delivering high-quality construction, facilities management, and technical solutions across North America. As a family-owned organization with a long-standing reputation for operational excellence, they are known for their collaborative culture, commitment to safety, and focus on building lasting client relationships. With a diverse project portfolio spanning healthcare, infrastructure, and commercial sectors, Black & McDonald continues to be a trusted partner for complex and impactful projects

## Role Description:

Reporting to the Division Manager, the Electrical Project Manager will be responsible for overseeing electrical construction projects from award through to completion, ensuring successful delivery aligned with scope, budget, schedule, and quality expectations. You will play a key role in coordinating cross-functional teams, managing financial performance, and maintaining strong client relationships while ensuring compliance with safety and regulatory standards.

By joining Black & McDonald, you will contribute to a diverse range of commercial and institutional projects, including healthcare and large-scale construction initiatives. You will work closely with experienced team members and leadership while leveraging tools such as Procore and enterprise accounting systems to manage project execution, forecasting, and reporting. Competitive compensation, including base salary, incentives, and a comprehensive benefits package, reflects the organization's commitment to attracting and retaining top talent.

## Your responsibilities will include:

• Overseeing project planning, scheduling, and execution from kickoff through closeout;

• Managing project financials, including budgeting, forecasting, and progress claims;

• Coordinating internal teams, subcontractors, and site personnel to ensure alignment;

• Reviewing drawings, specifications, and shop documentation to support project delivery;

• Managing change orders and ensuring accurate documentation and approvals;

• Maintaining ongoing communication with clients, stakeholders, and project partners;

• Ensuring compliance with safety regulations and quality standards on all projects;

• Utilizing project management and financial systems for tracking and reporting;

• Supporting job setup, resource allocation, and continuous process improvement.

## Your Qualifications:

As the ideal candidate, you are a driven and detail-oriented project management professional with strong electrical knowledge and a passion for delivering high-quality construction projects. You bring a proactive mindset, strong communication skills, and commitment to integrity and teamwork. Whether you have progressed through a trade background or developed your experience through construction management, you are eager to grow your career within a supportive and collaborative environment.

Your qualifications will include:

• 5+ years of experience managing electrical or construction projects within commercial or institutional environments;

• Strong understanding of electrical systems, codes, and industry standards;

• Proven ability to manage budgets, schedules, and project risks;

• Experience reading and interpreting drawings and technical documentation;

• Proficiency with project management tools such as Procore and ERP systems;

• Strong communication, leadership, and stakeholder management skills;

• Ability to manage change orders, claims, and contract requirements;

