2234359.description:
At CBCL, we pride ourselves on being a dynamic and innovative leader in engineering and environmental consulting. We're driven by creativity, collaboration, and a passion for excellence – qualities that enable us to deliver exceptional solutions for our clients. If you're ready to take on meaningful challenges and make an impact, we'd love to have you join our team!

Our Water Resources & Climate Change Department has an opportunity for an Intermediate Water Resources Engineer to bring their expertise and enthusiasm to our company. This position may be based out of our Halifax, NS; Fredericton, NB; Moncton, NB; or Saint John, NB office.

In this dynamic role, you'll contribute to solving critical water resources and stormwater management challenges. Whether you're assisting with flood and erosion studies, sewer system analysis, or supporting the development of stormwater management solutions, your work will help create sustainable and resilient communities—both here in Canada and globally.

As our ideal candidate, you are a results-driven professional with a strong technical foundation and a passion for delivering effective water resource solutions. You excel in both independent work and collaborative team settings. You have a solid background in hydrologic and hydraulic modeling and are eager to take on increasing project responsibilities while continuing to develop your technical expertise.

Your key responsibilities:

• Support water resources and stormwater management projects, including flood studies, hydraulic structure assessments and sizing, concept design development, stormwater separation and master planning, and climate change assessments;

• Conduct hydrologic and hydraulic modeling for urban infrastructure (1D, dual drainage, 1D-2D), transportation drainage systems, and floodplain mapping, among others;

• Assist in the development of stormwater management strategies to mitigate flooding, protect the environment, and address climate resilience;

• Prepare project deliverables, including models/designs, calculations, opinion of probable cost;

• Manage projects or oversee technical teams to keep projects on schedule and budget;

• Collaborate with multidisciplinary teams to deliver high-quality solutions that meet client and regulatory requirements; and

• Engage in professional development and contribute to the mentorship of junior team members while growing your own expertise.

Your capabilities & credentials:

• Undergraduate Degree in Civil, Water Resources, Environmental, or Coastal Engineering (equivalent combination of education and experience will also be considered);

• 5+ years of relevant experience in water resources or stormwater management field;

• Professional Engineer (P.Eng.) designation in Canada;

• Experience supporting projects as a technical contributor, with a desire to develop project management and client relationship skills;

• Proficiency with hydrologic and hydraulic modeling tools, such as PCSWMM, HEC-RAS, or equivalent software; and

• A collaborative mindset with a commitment to professional growth and continuous learning.

Additional skills and experience that will make you stand out:

• Experience in technical oversight and/or mentorship of junior engineers would be considered a strong asset;

• Experience in Atlantic Canada would be considered a strong asset; and

• Background in engineering consulting, particularly in water resource and stormwater management projects would be considered a strong asset.

You are welcome to apply even if you do not meet all of the requirements.

What we can offer you:

• A competitive compensation package effective on your first day of employment:
• Comprehensive health and dental benefits

