2239986.description:
Oberland Agriscience Inc. is a sustainable black soldier fly larvae (BSFL) farm in Halifax, NS. We are dedicated to closing the food loop in our region and making a positive contribution to our planet. Oberland's high-performing team rears BSFL in our zero-waste facility, delivering exceptional productivity per hectare and yielding nutrient-rich, low-environmental impact products.

Partnering with local food producers and distributors, Oberland upcycles organic waste and food production by-products such as spent grains from local craft breweries to grow BSFL on an industrial scale. Oberland actively plays a role in a more sustainable circular economy in Atlantic Canada. Oberland generates high-quality sustainable protein products from the larvae, marketed and sold under the Obie's BSFL brand, and is seeking certification on an insect-derived fertilizer product for home gardens and agricultural lands.

Position Title: Production Supervisor
Department: Operations
Reports To: VP Operations
Full-Time - averaging 42 Hours/Week (4 -on/4-off rotation)

Location: 71 Grassy Lake Drive, Halifax NS

Job Summary
The Production Supervisor is responsible for overseeing daily manufacturing operations within the agriscience production facility. This role ensures production targets are met safely, efficiently, and in compliance with quality, environmental, and regulatory standards. The supervisor leads production staff, drives continuous improvement, and supports a culture of safety, accountability, and operational excellence.

## Key Responsibilities

• Supervise and coordinate daily production activities to meet safety, quality, delivery, and cost goals;

• Lead, train, and develop production employees (through Team Leads); manage staffing, scheduling, and performance;

• Ensure compliance with GMP, OH&S, ECCC, and company safety and environmental standards;

• Monitor production metrics and address issues related to downtime, yield, and efficiency;

• Enforce standard operating procedures (SOPs) and work instructions;

• Collaborate with Quality, Maintenance, OHS, and Supply Chain teams to resolve production issues;

• Investigate and respond to safety incidents, quality deviations, and equipment failures;

• Support continuous improvement initiatives;

• Participate in audits, inspections, and regulatory reviews;

• Ensure accurate documentation, batch records, and production reports;

• Support team in preparing for facility tours, lead tours as needed;

## Skills & Competencies

• Strong leadership and people-management skills

• Excellent problem-solving and decision-making abilities

• Clear verbal and written communication

• Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment

• Data-driven mindset with focus on continuous improvement

• Intermediate proficiency in Microsoft Office (Excel, Word, Outlook) with the ability to analyze production data and prepare reports.

## Qualifications

• High school diploma or GED required; Degree in Manufacturing, Engineering, Agriscience, or related field considered an asset.

• 1+ years of supervisory experience in a manufacturing environment

• Experience in regulated manufacturing (agriscience, chemical, food, pharmaceutical, or similar)

• Strong understanding of safety regulations and manufacturing best practices

• Fluent in English reading, writing and comprehension

This job description is not intended to be all-inclusive. The employee may be required to perform other related duties as assigned to meet the ongoing needs of the organization.

Send applications to Careers@Oberlandag.com

2174538.description:
With more than 50 years of Aerospace industry experience, IMP Aerostructures, an Operating Unit of IMP Aerospace and Defence, is a leader in the Aerospace industry providing top quality, structural components and assemblies to clients such as Bombardier, Bell Helicopter, Boeing, Spirit Aerosystems and Lockheed. Located in the quaint town of Amherst, NS, just a short trip from Moncton, NB, you'll enjoy a lifestyle that offers all of the amenities of big city living in a rural setting. Recognized as one of Canada's Best Managed Companies, IMP Group takes enormous pride in the diligence and hard work its employee groups provide. Known for providing its employees with a supportive and challenging atmosphere, fostering growth and personal development, IMP Aerostructures has an immediate opening for a motivated individual to join its winning team!

Position Overview:
Responsible to interpret customer manufacturing instructions and technical drawing or digital data packages to transcribe the requirements into the manufacturing plans (routing and bills of material) in accordance with customer process and quality requirements. An aerospace methods planner is essentially the bridge between engineering design and the factory floor. They should possess the ability and training to take a design on paper (or CAD) and then determine the "how to implement" — the exact sequence, tooling, materials, and processes needed to build it efficiently, safely, and to specification.These are to be achieved to ensure product safety using the most economical manufacturing method for the fabrication of aircraft/aerospace details and assemblies that adhere to customer requirements.

What You Will Do:
• Provide estimates for quoting requirements including work flow, equipment and tooling requirements, materials and special processes which may require outside production.

• Interact with Supervisor by communicating and receiving instruction in the transition of quoting/estimating to onboarding of new work to implement the workflow, current material needs, equipment and/or to address the manufacturing methodology/potential problems accordingly.

• Review customer technical data package, engineering, specifications to ensure accurate and safe part manufacture in item routings.

• Develop and maintain item numbers (manufactured, purchased and outside production), production routings and bill-of-material for the efficient manufacture of aircraft component parts to the specified configuration.

• Create and maintain the 'Item Masters and Item Branch' records in JD Edwards per applicable procedures.

• Ensure proper configuration control is defined of all component parts, outside operation, purchased materials and tooling.

• Work collaboratively with Quality Engineering and Manufacturing Engineering Technicians to implement changes, reworks and/or alternate processing requirements.

• Provide support to Customer Representative Representatives (i.e. Contracts), Quality Assurance and applicable Production Areas in order to resolve configuration and/or technical issues and their respective implementation.

• Identify Tooling, Shop Drawing and First Article Inspection (FAI) requirements and update 'lock notes'.

• Review shop drawings for the fabrication of aircraft/aerospace details in accordance with the configuration defined by planning.

• Participate in implementing corrective actions derived from NCR disposition, CAR action resolution and audit finding implementation requirements

• Maintain and wear all personal protective equipment (PPE) applicable to the area you will be in or the operation or task you are about to conduct. Maintain a clear-shaven face at all times during any activity regarding the use of a respirator.

• Become familiar with applicable safety data sheets (SDS), safe work procedures and/or regulations affecting the work and/or this workplace.

• Adhere to workplace safety policies, regulations and the use safety equipment will be the highest priority for you and your co-workers.

What You Will Bring:
• Completion of High School (Grade 12) and;

• Completion of a 2-yr Manufacturing Engineering Technologist Diploma;

• Completion of an aircraft blueprint/GD&T course or demonstrated ability in interpreting aircraft blueprints/CATIA models and understanding of GD&T;

• Good knowledge and ability to use MS Office, specifically Excel (pivot tables) and ERP systems;

• Excellent reading interpretation and comprehension across multi-level specification requirements;

• Strong analytical, visual concepts and math skills required;

• Strong organizational skills for record keeping and historical traceability and audit retrieval;

• Must complete a criminal check to be in this position to be eligible to access customer technical data websites;

• Must be eligible to meet the requirements for Canadian Controlled Goods Program (CGP) and the Canadian Security Clearances;

• Must be able to work co-operatively with others and follow directives precisely;

• Knowledge of processes, products and equipment will be considered an asset;

• Completion of Global Harmonized System (WHMIS) course;

• Must meet physical requirements of the position including but not limited to: walking, static standing and leg/foot movement for extended periods, bending, stooping, squatting, twisting/trunk rotation, weight bearing / lifting, carrying, pushing & pulling heavy objects; hand/wrist gripping, grasping, pinching, vibration depend on tasks/tools, neck & back flexion;

• Adhere to, and demonstrate a personal commitment to IMP Occupational Health, Safety and Environment Policies. Continually focusing on your individual safety and the safety of others who may be affected by your work and to fully comply with all Nova Scotia Provincial Health, Safety and Environment Legislation.

What We Will Do For You:
