• Bachelor's Degree in Electrical Engineering from an accredited university;

• Registered as a P.Eng. (or eligible for registration as an Engineer-in-Training or P.Eng.) with Engineers Nova Scotia, APEGNB, or another Canadian engineering association;

• 4 years of relevant consulting engineering experience;

• Strong experience designing building electrical systems within a consulting engineering environment;

• Proficiency with AutoCAD and Revit; experience with AGi32, SKM PowerTools, or similar electrical analysis software is considered an asset;

• Demonstrated ability to manage multiple projects, prioritize competing deadlines, and deliver high-quality work;

• Experience coordinating multidisciplinary projects and mentoring junior team members is considered an asset;

• Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English; bilingualism in French is considered an asset;

• Valid driver's license with the ability to travel to project sites as required.

