2236113.description:
Director, Total Rewards
Halifax or New Glasgow, NS; Mississauga, ON
AM - CRR - 9901

Meridia Recruitment Solutions is proud to have partnered with Crombie in the recruitment of their new Director, Total Rewards.

Crombie is one of Canada's leading real estate investment trusts, owning and operating a diversified portfolio of high-quality properties across the country. Headquartered in Nova Scotia, the organization is driven by integrity, collaboration, and a commitment to creating spaces that strengthen communities and generate long-term value. With a national presence, a strong culture, and a focus on sustainable growth, Crombie puts their people at the heart of the business. As one of Atlantic Canada's Top Employers, Crombie continues to invest in its people, communities, and future.

## Role Description

As Director, Total Rewards, you will provide leadership in the design, development, implementation, and evaluation of compensation and reward programs and policies across the organization. Reporting to the Senior Director, People & Culture, you will partner closely with senior leadership to develop innovative, competitive, and cost-effective total rewards strategies that support Crombie's business objectives, employee value proposition, and long-term organizational success. This role combines strategic leadership with hands-on execution and oversight of programs supporting both employees, executives, and our Board of Trustees.

By joining Crombie, you will play a critical role in shaping and evolving the organization's total rewards philosophy, compensation structures, employee and executive reward programs, and payroll and benefits functions. You will lead key initiatives related to job architecture, market benchmarking, executive compensation governance, data analytics, and program optimization while collaborating with leaders across the business. Crombie offers a competitive compensation package including short-term and long-term incentive opportunities, comprehensive benefits, a Defined Contribution Pension Plan, wellness support, and professional development opportunities.

## Your responsibilities will include:

• Developing and executing a comprehensive total rewards strategy aligned with Crombie's business objectives and talent priorities;

• Leading the design, implementation, and continuous improvement of compensation, benefits, payroll, retirement, incentive, and recognition programs;

• Managing compensation philosophy, salary structures, pay equity initiatives, annual compensation reviews, and job architecture frameworks;

• Designing, administering, and evaluating executive compensation programs and policies including short-term and long-term incentive plans;

• Conducting market intelligence, benchmarking, and compensation analysis to ensure external competitiveness and internal equity;

• Preparing recommendations, disclosures, reports, and governance materials for executive leadership, Board committees, and key stakeholders;

• Overseeing payroll and benefits (delivered by third-party), vendor relationships, and related systems while ensuring compliance with applicable regulations;

• Leveraging analytics, reporting, and financial insights to support workforce planning, budgeting, forecasting, and strategic decision-making;

• Providing leadership, coaching, and subject matter expertise while building strong relationships with internal and external stakeholders across the organization.

## Your Qualifications

As the ideal candidate, you are a strategic and results-oriented total rewards leader with deep expertise across compensation, benefits, payroll, executive rewards, and analytics. You bring strong financial and business acumen and the ability to balance organizational objectives with employee needs while building credibility with executives, boards, and business leaders. Comfortable operating in a hands-on environment, you are a collaborative and influential professional who can translate complex information into meaningful insights and recommendations that drive action.

Qualifications include:

• Bachelor's degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, Finance, or a related discipline, or an equivalent combination of education and experience;

• 8-10+ years of progressive experience in compensation, benefits, payroll, and total rewards, including leadership experience;

• Demonstrated expertise designing and implementing comprehensive total rewards programs in complex organizations;

• Experience managing executive compensation programs and supporting Boards, Compensation Committees, or executive leadership teams;

• Strong knowledge of compensation strategy, job evaluation, job architecture, market benchmarking, and pay equity practices;

• Advanced analytical and financial acumen with the ability to interpret data and develop actionable recommendations;

• Proven project management and change leadership capabilities;

• Exceptional communication, relationship-building, and stakeholder management skills with the ability to influence at all levels;

• CCP, CEBS, CPHR, or another relevant professional designation would be considered a strong asset. • Advanced Microsoft skills leveraging Excel and PowerPoint and other related technologies.

To express interest in this opportunity please apply online by clicking "Apply Now" below.

For more information contact Austin McLennan, Partner, at 902-424-1103 and amclennan@kbrs.ca or Abdul Dalloul, Recruitment Specialist at 902-334-7488 and adalloul@kbrs.ca, or please apply online by clicking the "Apply Now" button below. If you require accommodation to participate in the recruitment process, please let Austin or Abdul know.

Meridia Recruitment Solutions connects leading organizations with top talent by building strong relationships and creating ideal matches with candidates because we are only successful when you are. We appreciate your interest in this opportunity.

To learn more about Meridia Recruitment Solutions, our job opportunities, and career advice we invite you to explore our site and subscribe for career alerts.

2239857.description:
## Property Manager
Halifax, NS
AM - HHP - 9695

Meridia Recruitment Solutions has partnered with Halifax Harbour Properties (HHP), a community-focused, family owned business, to recruit a Property Manager to join their growing property management team.

HHP is dedicated to providing comfortable, affordable, and well-maintained properties within the Halifax Regional Municipality, focusing on convenience, livability, and community connection. Driven by a mission to become one of the leading property management teams in the region, HHP has a portfolio of centrally located residential and multi-unit apartment buildings situated in urban, walkable neighborhoods, many within or close to downtown Halifax and downtown Dartmouth. With a strong commitment to exceptional client relationships and high standards of service, offering employees the opportunity to contribute to a growing portfolio while making a real difference in the communities they serve.

## Role Description:

Reporting directly to the General Manager, the Property Manager will oversee the daily operations of the portfolio, including supervising on-site staff, conducting regular property inspections, coordinating maintenance and repairs, and ensuring buildings are clean, safe, and well-maintained. The role involves managing tenant relations and resolving escalated issues, overseeing leasing and rent collection processes, and ensuring compliance with all applicable residential tenancy regulations. In addition, you will also approve expenses, and coordinate capital projects, while handling vendor relationships and responding to emergencies as needed.

By joining HHP, you will be part of a growing, family-owned, and community-oriented property management company. You will have the opportunity to improve on existing property management practices, as well as support the implementation of new practices and technologies, all within a collaborative and supportive environment. In return for your skills and expertise, you will be rewarded with a competitive compensation and benefits package.

Your responsibilities will include:

• Drive operational excellence by leading site teams, setting standards and workflows, enforcing accountability, conducting inspections, and making timely decisions on repairs and procedures;

• Oversee maintenance and capital planning through preventive programs, effective work order management, project coordination, vendor negotiations, and regulatory compliance;

• Manage tenant relations by resolving complex issues with clear documentation, fair enforcement, and professional communication that protects ownership interests;

• Oversee property administration by ensuring accurate, compliant lease processes, approving documentation, and maintaining audit-ready records;

• Lead and develop staff through recruitment, training, performance management, scheduling, and adherence to SOPs and safety standards;

• Manage tenancy and legal matters by interpreting legislation, handling applications and hearings, preparing documentation, coordinating enforcement, and advising on risk.

## Your Qualifications:

As the ideal candidate, you are an experienced Property Manager who has successfully managed a portfolio of residential properties. You are a driven, organized, and approachable individual who brings forward comprehensive knowledge of property management best practices, and tenancy regulations. You are also technologically inclined and have an eye for creating efficiencies to support streamlined property management practices across the business.

Qualifications include:

• 5+ years of professional experience managing a multi-unit residential, affordable housing, or condominium portfolio;

• Post-secondary education in a relevant discipline (i.e., business, real estate, property management) would be considered a strong asset;

• Strong working knowledge of property management systems (i.e., Yardi), accounting software, and Microsoft Office suite;

• Proficient in preparing weekly/ monthly/ quarterly operational reports for the senior management, presenting both written reports and verbal summaries in management meetings, including escalation of high-risk issues requiring executive attention;

• Exceptional communication, problem-solving, decision-making, and customer service abilities;

• Organized multi-tasker with a keen eye for detail and ability to remain calm under pressure;

• Working knowledge of building systems, maintenance, and capital planning.

To express interest in this opportunity please apply online by clicking "Apply Now" below.

For more information contact Austin McLennan, Partner, at 902-424-1103 and amclennan@kbrs.ca or please apply online by clicking the "Apply Now" button below. If you require accommodation to participate in the recruitment process, please let Austin know.

