CBCL is seeking an Intermediate or Senior Mechanical Engineer to join our Industrial Engineering team based in Fredericton, NB!

Join us and help shape both our work environment and company culture by collaborating with other design and construction professionals on challenging and exciting industrial projects. From concept to completion, bring your passion for sustainable design principles to life while delivering exceptional results for our clients.

As our ideal candidate you have hands-on industry experience in project engineering or technical roles, or as a consultant designing industrial mechanical systems. This includes expertise in pulp and paper, manufacturing, process fluid systems, stress analysis, petrochemical storage and transfer, storage tanks, compressed gas systems, boilers, power plants, or other industrial systems. Experience supporting mill operations, equipment upgrades, maintenance reliability, shutdown planning, commissioning, or process optimization in pulp and paper environments would be considered a strong asset.

Your Key Responsibilities:

• Support or lead design projects for pulp and paper, industry, manufacturing, energy transitions, fuel storage, natural gas, pipelines, power plants, and boiler systems, ensuring technical excellence, quality, and client satisfaction;

