Reporting to the Manager, Financial Reporting, the Accounting Analyst plays a key role in the production of accurate, high-quality financial information. Through participation in accounting operations, account reconciliations, and the preparation of financial statements, this individual contributes directly to the organization's performance. This opportunity is ideal for a detail-oriented, analytical professional who is motivated to develop their expertise within a collaborative team in the insurance industry.

Qualifications
To be successful in this role, the incumbent should possess the following qualifications:

• Bachelor's degree in accounting or finance, or a post-secondary diploma combined with a few years of relevant experience;

• Strong knowledge of accounting principles, including journal entries, chart of accounts, general ledger, and financial statements;

• Good understanding of the accounting cycle and accounting information systems;

• Strong attention to detail and accuracy, with a disciplined approach to applying procedures and internal controls;

• Advanced proficiency in Excel for the preparation, analysis, and validation of financial data;

• Bilingualism required (French and English, both written and spoken);

