At CBCL Limited, we are a successful, dynamic, and growing engineering and environmental consulting firm. We have an exciting opportunity for an Intermediate to Senior Electrical Engineer to join our Electrical & Instrumentation team based in either Halifax, Nova Scotia or Fredericton, New Brunswick. Bring your expertise, creativity, and leadership to a team that thrives on delivering excellence in electrical design and consulting for a wide range of industrial, water, wastewater, and infrastructure projects. You'll play a key role in shaping the future of essential infrastructure across diverse sectors, all while being part of a supportive, collaborative team dedicated to technical excellence and client satisfaction.

Your Key Responsibilities:

• Lead and Innovate: Manage, coordinate, and design electrical systems for industrial facilities, water & wastewater treatment plants, pump stations, and other infrastructure;

• Mentor and Inspire: Provide leadership and mentorship to junior engineers and technologists, fostering an environment that encourages innovation and growth;

• Design with Precision: Prepare detailed designs, contract documents, and technical specifications for systems such as power distribution (medium and low voltage), lighting, telecommunications, fire alarm, instrumentation, control systems;

• Deliver Excellence: Provide electrical engineering advice and support across multidisciplinary teams, ensuring smooth project execution and technical excellence;

• Ensure Safety & Quality: Incorporate safety standards and risk analysis into designs while ensuring projects adhere to electrical codes, standards, and best practices;

• Drive Business Growth: Engage in business development activities, including proposal preparation and client interaction; and

• Provide On-Site Expertise: Conduct site surveys, assess existing infrastructure, and oversee construction activities to ensure the successful execution of projects.

Your Capabilities and Credentials:

• A degree in Electrical Engineering is required, with registration or eligibility for registration with provincial Engineering Associations;

• Minimum of 7 years of relevant electrical engineering experience;

• Experience in electrical system design, including power distribution, lighting, control systems, and instrumentation, with in-depth knowledge of electrical codes;

• Proficiency in Revit for electrical design, coordination, and interdisciplinary project collaboration;

• Strong communication skills to effectively convey technical information, draft detailed reports, and work collaboratively with clients, multidisciplinary teams, and project stakeholders; and

• Strong organizational and time management skills to meet deadlines and deliver quality work on time and within budget.

You are welcome to apply even if you do not meet all of the requirements.

Valued Experience

• Experience working in a consulting engineering environment is preferred;

• 10+ years of relevant electrical engineering experience;

• Electrical design experience in industrial, water, and/or wastewater; and

• Knowledge of PLC-based control systems and instrumentation.

• The ability to communicate in both English and French would be an asset.

What we can offer you:

• A competitive compensation package effective on your first day of employment:
• Comprehensive health and dental benefits

• CAAT Defined Benefit Pension Plan with employer contributions

• Generous vacation allowance commensurate with experience

• Maternity or Parental leave top-up

• Health spending account

• Wellness incentive

• Membership dues reimbursement

• Education and lifelong learning subsidization

• Community volunteering incentive

