• Diploma in Electrical Engineering Technology, Electrical and Electronics Engineering Technology, or a related discipline from an accredited institution;

• Minimum 5 to 10 years of experience in electrical design, drafting, or field services within the consulting, construction, or engineering industry;

• Eligibility for, or registration as, a Professional Technologist (P.Tech.) designation is considered an asset;

• Strong understanding of building electrical systems, including power distribution, emergency power, lighting, fire alarm, communications, and low-voltage systems;

• Working knowledge of applicable electrical codes, standards, and industry best practices;

• Proficiency with AutoCAD and Revit for electrical design and drafting;

• Experience with electrical analysis and design software such as AGi32, SKM, ETAP, or similar tools is considered an asset;

