Reporting to the Primary Health Care Directorate, the incumbent possesses extensive expertise and experience in streamlining operations and resources. They provide strong leadership and support the transformation of the health care system toward a primary health care–focused model, in alignment with the strategic plan, with a view to system optimization, effectiveness, and efficiency. In collaboration with directors, managers, and partners, the incumbent leads successful change by managing complex improvement projects, analyzing current workflows, identifying opportunities for improvement, and designing, developing, evaluating, and implementing change initiatives using advanced improvement strategies and techniques. They develop a lean operating model within a clinical environment by leveraging data at all stages of the care pathway, along with in-depth analysis and close monitoring of performance indicators. They work with various stakeholders to identify barriers, streamline processes, and implement innovative solutions for the use of community-based services and resources, as well as to optimize functional processes and ensure smooth transitions with specialized services, including hospitals. The incumbent plays a critical role in optimizing the allocation and utilization of human resources within our facilities and must be motivated to help the organization achieve excellence in person-centered care while maintaining an efficient and effective approach.

