2228007.description:
## LARGE VESSEL - ENGINEER

Kelly Cove Salmon Ltd., a division of Cooke Aquaculture Inc., a dynamic and growing east coast family company, with Platinum Member status in the Canada's Best Managed Companies Program, is offering a unique opportunity for a highly motivated individual to join the Company's Large Vessel Team as Vessel Engineer. This position reports to the Captain.

Cooke is a global seafood company with operations in North America, Europe, and South America. Our company's success is driven by our dynamic, highly-skilled and innovative management team, supported by dedicated employees who live in coastal communities and contribute to the local area's economy and sense of community.

## The Role:

As a result of our robust growth, we are expanding our team of professionals. The key role of this position is to monitor and operate the vessel's mechanical equipment.

## Primary duties are (not limited to):

• Safe and economical operations of all machinery on the vessel;

• Proper maintenance of all machinery on the vessel;

• Performs troubleshooting, problem solving as well as preventative and corrective maintenance to prevent down time and to ensure the efficient and continual functioning of the vessel;

• Environmental management

• Monitoring of bunkers and lubricants;

• Maintain accurate records and other duties as assigned.

## Qualifications/Requirements/Attributes:

• Fourth - Class Engineer Certificate issued by Transport Canada;

• SCTW Motor Certificate;

• Strong in sense of responsibility and pride in overall condition of machinery;

• Strong organizational, communication and interpersonal skills;

• Experienced with Safety Management Systems;

• Valid Marine Basic First Aid or Advanced First Aid and CPR;

• Valid Seafarers Medical Certificate;

• Valid Canadian Passport with the ability to enter the US;

• A certification in the Transportation of Dangerous Goods will be considered an asset.

• As per company policy, a clear result of a pre-employment criminal background check.

•

Salary commensurate with experience which includes a competitive health and dental benefit package.

