2240542.description:
## Arena Attendant I

## (Permanent, Full-time)

## Department of Recreation & Community Safety

## $33.33/hour

## Join one of Newfoundland and Labrador's premier recreation facilities.

The City of Mount Pearl is seeking a motivated and dependable 4th Class Power Engineer to join our team as an Arena Attendant I. The position is based out of the Glacier - one of the busiest and most environmentally friendly arena facilities in the province. Our facility hosts major hockey tournaments, figure skating competitions, trade shows, and community events throughout the year, creating an exciting and dynamic work environment.

This is an excellent opportunity for someone looking to build a rewarding career in arena operations while learning from some of the best professionals in the industry.

## Why Join Our Team?

Our Arena Attendants are known for their expertise, professionalism, and commitment to excellence. If you have your Class 4 Power Engineer Certificate, we can teach you the specialized skills required to succeed in arena operations and ice maintenance.

You'll have the opportunity to:

Work in a state-of-the-art recreation facility;

Learn ice-making and arena operations from an experienced and highly respected team;

Play an important role in hosting major sporting events, tournaments, trade shows, and community activities;

Build a long-term career in a supportive and team-oriented environment;

Bonus, you'll get to drive the ice resurfacer!

## What We Offer

The City of Mount Pearl provides an outstanding compensation and benefits package, including:

• Defined Benefit Pension Plan (cost-shared with the City);

• Group Benefits Program (cost-shared with the City);

• Paid Time Off;

• A complimentary gym membership;

• Free swimming and skating for you and your immediate family members.

## What We're Looking For

We're looking for individuals who are:

• Safety-conscious and reliable;

• Team-oriented and customer-focused;

• Willing to learn and take pride in their work;

• Comfortable working in a fast-paced environment;

• Interested in developing specialized skills in arena and facility operations.

## Required Qualification

• Class 4 Power Engineer Certificate

## Be Part of Something Bigger

Whether it's helping create championship-quality ice, preparing for a major trade show, or supporting community events that bring people together, you'll play a key role in delivering exceptional experiences for residents and visitors alike.

If you're ready to learn from the best and build a career with a progressive and growing municipality, we want to hear from you.

