2240608.description:
Position Type:
Permanent
*

Closing date:
2026-09-26
*

Medavie Health Services is a national leader in primary health care solutions and the largest contracted provider of emergency management services in Canada. Together with Medavie Blue Cross, we are part of Medavie, a health solutions partner committed to improving the wellbeing of Canadians.

With a growing network of 5,400 health care professionals in six provinces, Medavie Health Services has a long history of operating ground and air ambulance services, medical communications, Mobile Integrated Health/Community Paramedicine programs, 911 Public Safety, 811 Telehealth, home health care, as well as clinical training.

We are proud to invest in communities to help address some of Canada's most pressing physical and mental health care challenges.

As an employee of Medavie Health Services, we are accountable to our patients and coworkers by participating in and supporting all safety related initiatives, as well as acting in a manner that fosters a culture that focuses on patient safety and a safe and respectful workplace.

Reporting to the General Manager, the Operations Manager leads western operations and facility management for Island EMS and provides support to the Provincial MFR Program. Reporting to the General Manager, the role supports effective service delivery, staff development, and alignment with organizational policies and priorities.

Key accountabilities include staff and service improvement, facility maintenance, Medical First Responder programs, occupational health and safety, and operational policy development. The manager also promotes a culture of patient and workplace safety across IEMS.

As an employee of IEMS, we are accountable to our patients and coworkers by participating in and supporting all safety related initiatives, as well as acting in a manner that fosters a culture that focuses on patient safety and a safe workplace.

## The position entails, but is not limited to the following:

• Ongoing management and oversight of western operations and staff (Alberton, O'Leary and Summerside bases);

• Ongoing facility management and oversight of all IEMS facilities which includes working with employees, Duty SOPs, management and fleet staff to identify and address any issues;

• Manage employee and labour issues with utmost confidentiality, empathy, and respect;

• Prepare and distribute operational or facility updates and memos to all staff;

• Demonstrate superior conflict resolutions skills by balancing assertiveness, sensitivity and successfully mediating conflicts will be a key skill you will possess;

• Responsible for the safety and well-being of staff and the public ensuring that all regulations, guidelines, and legislation are followed;

• Provide support and oversight to the Provincial MFR Coordinator;

• Responsible for conducting investigations into any complaints or inquiries brought forward;

• Involved in the decision making of recruitment processes and candidate selection as well as other Human Resources recruitment functions;

• Working with the communications team for public information releases, serving as a representative of Island EMS at community, stakeholder or municipal meetings when required;

• Provides clinical support as well as coaching by attending scenes when required;

• This position may require working on the ambulance in emergencies to retain professional skills as a paramedic;

• Ensure overall responsibility and accountability of all aspects of the deployment and utilization of Paramedic resources, operational policies, and resources to maintain the efficiency and effectiveness of the service provided;

• Provide on scene coordination for major incidents, coordinate contingency and disaster management process;

