NOTE: Applicants must attach a resume to their application.

We are looking for a motivated orthopedic surgeon who wants to be part of a dynamic team, where mutual support, communication, and teamwork are essential to the quality of care we provide to our patients.

This is a general orthopedic surgery practice within a 160-bed regional hospital that houses most surgical specialties, including an 8-bed intensive care unit. This is an opportunity to contribute to the development of orthopedic services and to make a real difference in a community that offers an excellent quality of life in a region with exceptional access to outdoor activities and the ocean, all at an affordable cost of living.

## Your Main Responsibilities:

• Assess, diagnose, and treat various musculoskeletal conditions;

• Perform orthopedic surgical procedures in accordance with best practices;

• Provide pre- and post-operative care for patients;

• Work closely with members of the medical and interdisciplinary teams to provide high-quality care;

• Actively participate in the development and continuous improvement of clinical practice;

• Participate in regional on-call duty (typically 1 in 6 days to 1 in 8 days).

## Qualifications:

• Hold or be eligible for a regular or defined license to practice medicine in New Brunswick;

• Excellent clinical and surgical skills;

• A collaborative spirit and a desire to contribute to a team of four surgeons, where each member plays an important role;

• Excellent interpersonal and communication skills;

• Independence, professionalism, and a sense of responsibility;

• A patient-centered approach and a commitment to excellence in care;

• Training or a strong interest in sports orthopedics, particularly shoulder and knee surgery, is an asset;

• Fluency in French is an asset.

## Requirements:

• A degree from an accredited medical school and a residency leading to licensure in orthopedic surgery.

By "accredited medical school," we mean a school that meets the following criteria:

• Accredited by the Canadian Accreditation Committee of Medical Schools (CAFMC) or the Liaison Committee on Medical Education (LCME) (in the United States);

• Listed in the World Directory of Medical Schools and bearing a note from Canada.

OR

• Recognized certification in orthopedic surgery from the Royal College of Physicians and Surgeons of Canada.

AND

• Hold a license from the College of Physicians and Surgeons of New Brunswick;

• Be an active member of the Canadian Medical Protective Association or an association offering equivalent liability insurance;

• Be a member of the New Brunswick Medical Society;

• Hold privileges with the Vitalité Health Network;

• Be registered with New Brunswick Health Insurance;

• Experience (one to three years) is considered an asset;

